Defines all measurable units (pieces, kg, liters, hours, boxes, etc.) and their conversion rules between units in the same category.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Product sales, purchase, and inventory in different units
Automatic unit conversion on orders, deliveries, and BOMs
Pricing per unit (e.g. sell by box, buy by kg)
Recipe / BOM quantities with different UoMs
Invoicing and reporting in preferred units
Time tracking (hours, days) and service products
Packaging and logistics units

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent, core)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), category_id → uom.category (required)
uom_type (reference / bigger / smaller)
factor, factor_inv (conversion ratio)
rounding (float, e.g. 0.01)
active, company_id
measure_type (unit / weight / volume / time / etc.)

Critical Hooks: onchange_category_id, _compute_factor, conversion engine (_compute_quantity)
Security: Generally read-access for all, write restricted to settings managers

RAG Routing Keywords:
unit of measure, uom, uom.uom, measure unit, conversion unit, pieces, kg, liter, box, pack, hour, unit category, uom category, measurement unit
Related Models (most joined):

uom.category (parent category)
product.template / product.product (uom_id, uom_po_id)
sale.order.line, purchase.order.line, stock.move
mrp.bom.line
account.move.line

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
uom.uom is Odoo’s Unit of Measure model that stores units with name, category_id, conversion factor, rounding, and type (bigger/smaller/reference). It enables automatic quantity conversion across sales, purchase, inventory, manufacturing, and accounting, and is referenced on almost every product and transactional line in the system.